-- title:
--   Special-fibre points with stalk of dimension ≤ 1
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundle of data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` (the pushout of the two affine charts of the full modular function field in level $p$ with respect to Igusa's $j$) and its structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$: properness, flatness and integrality of that morphism and scheme, normality of its affine sections, curve models over $\mathbb{Q}$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with base changes together with their Galois and place compatibilities, two sections `εinf`, `εzero` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, a smooth locus, and further components summarised here, among them the curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\,\kappa$ over a field $\kappa$ and the two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$, $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ from its underlying scheme into the base change of `DRModel p` to $\kappa$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $toκ : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $z$ be a point of the pullback $\mathfrak{X}_O$ of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ which does not lie in the preimage under the second projection of the basic open set $D(p) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} O$, and assume that the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ at $z$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. Then $z$ is the image of the generic point of $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\,\kappa).C$ under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` (the map of pullbacks induced by the identity on `DRModel p` and $\operatorname{Spec}(toκ)$ on the base), or its image under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ followed by the same map.
--
--   This is the codimension statement for the Deligne–Rapoport model of the modular curve of level $p$ after base change to a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$: the only points of the special fibre whose local rings have dimension at most one are the generic points of the two components, the images of the $\infty$- and $0$-components. It is used in the verification of the codimension hypothesis [`V3Asm.codim`](thm.html#V3Asm.codim).
